{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1338130-question-about-animal-companion-and-spirits","id":1338130,"title":"Question about animal companion and spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-27T06:09:49-07:00","id":1338130,"title":"Question about animal companion and spirits","content":"I am working on my first werewolf game and one of my players wants to take a wolf companion. My question is in the Hisil does the spirit of the wolf has a seperate consiousness and it's like have 2 different allies one in the physical world and one in the hisil? And is the wolf spirit is fed more wolf spirits and spirits of the hunt does the physical wolf grow stronger and bigger? Should i treat the wolf with similar rules as to a physical mage familiar?<br /> <br /> Also in the book the pack, their are stories of totems possessing wolf companions and getting beefed up, if the wolf spirit is active can the totem still go in the wolf? Or does the wolf spirit fuse with the physical wolf ? <br /> <br /> Also i have a totem question, does the totem have a physical reflection or a form? My players were thinking of taking a spirit of a storm, could it inhabit a crow and fly around in the physical world with theme<br /> <br /> Thank you for your help and for the curious this os the setting i am working on<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333788-dark-eras-viking-setting\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333788-dark-eras-viking-setting\"> Dark eras : viking setting - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333788-dark-eras-viking-setting\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333788-dark-eras-viking-setting </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So i am storytelling a game werewolf game in the dark eras viking setting and wanted to shoot some ideas by reddit and get some feed back or ideas and just start a discussion. I was thinking taking some inspiration from the new God of war game and having a helion ridden who thinks/is the avatar of Baldur as main antagonist. He learn by going in the roots of the world tree that Ragnarok will never happen and is trying to force it by forcing the hand of the sons of Fenris (werewolves) to kill him. (P.98 of shun by the moon for inspiration) In the root of the world tree he allied him self with </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T09:41:36-07:00","id":1338153,"title":"","content":"1) Spirits are independent of what spawned them. Only very young spirits remain by the phenomenom that first made them come into being - yes, the spirit is a separate entity from the wolf. It may be miles away, or not even awakened yet. Is the character taking the wolf's spirit as a spiritual touchstone? Consider giving the wolf a tell to model it the spirit's antics.<br /> <br /> 2) Spirits aren't limited to cannibalism in order to sustain their predation - anything that you can symbolically link to a wolf can sustain it: from prey spirits, to conceptual spirits we've established with the wolf. Predation, fear, violence. In fact, a diverse diet from resonance related to their original concepts is what spirits require to become mature (ascend to rank 3 and above) - Don't confuse this with going Magath - the difference is the essence consumes has no symbolic link whatsoever to their original states.<br /> <br /> 3) There's a rite or gift that allows a pack totem to claim another member of their pack for a scene. I don't remember which from the top of my head.<br /> <br /> 4) Like I said in 1) spirits don't require to remain or protect what initially spawned them. In fact, most spirits come into being from the trauma of their dwellings being destroyed. Totems can't keep a totemic bond and claim a vessel at the same time (without the short-lived power mentioned in #3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T14:23:12-07:00","id":1338691,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the answers clears thing up a lot, but i am still wondering, don't totems have something that ties them to the physical world? Like an object or place? In dark eras it says that some totem have trouble going raiding because they are attached to a place or object. Maybe i am reading it wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T15:00:26-07:00","id":1338696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightsyko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1338130-question-about-animal-companion-and-spirits?p=1338691#post1338691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the answers clears thing up a lot, but i am still wondering, don't totems have something that ties them to the physical world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pack totems are literally <i>more</i> mobile than spirits without a pack bond, between the ability to treat every member of their pack as Resonant and being immune to Essence bleed. The Dark Eras section is there talking about the more prosaic issues that, if your pack is bound to a spirit of a singular thing (e.g. many <i>hursih</i> and <i>hursah</i> like the Forsaken often take as totems), a spirit whose nature makes it ill-suited for travel (e.g. the spirit of a local building), or a spirit that has fettered itself to an object (such as the ships, as mentioned in the section), then it will probably find it difficult (potentially impossible) to gain sustenance or provide meaningful assistance on a raid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T22:06:11-07:00","id":1342874,"title":"","content":"In Tales from the 13th Precinct there's a dog that has been Claimed by its own spirit. It's a police dog, and now it's a supernaturally powered one that's also pretty dedicated to its owner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T14:54:50-07:00","id":1343280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1338130-question-about-animal-companion-and-spirits?p=1342874#post1342874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Tales from the 13th Precinct there's a dog that has been Claimed by its own spirit. It's a police dog, and now it's a supernaturally powered one that's also pretty dedicated to its owner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how a werewolf would feel about that? Does a wolf ridden get a pass if the spirit inside is also a wolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T17:38:37-07:00","id":1343310,"title":"","content":"While there's a lot of options for fanatical characters, its not really a forced issue. There's not a lot of things you could get every Forsaken to agree upon.<br /> <br /> It's probably safe to say most werewolves who encountered it would think the worst, but there are werewolves who have claimed in their packs or might encourage it (some aware of the danger, some woefully naive). And it being a wolf spirit might lend some more sympathy to a werewolf.<br /> <br /> The dog-spirit claiming example has already done some stuff (namely, killing those it deemed &quot;intruders&quot; and hidden their bodies). It can get especially dangerous with animal claimed because the creature may for a while still look like a version of its animal, albeit a creepy or striking version, but have a level of understanding, as well as physical ability, that goes well beyond an animal normally should. All while maintaining the needs and desires of a twisted and predatory version of the animal.<br /> <br /> There's some movies about this kind of thing. Not specifically claimed, but someone finding an animal, taking it in, and realizing too late that it has some sort of supernatural levels of intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-23-2019, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}